  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'The Beginners Method offers a straightforward approach to solving the
    Rubik''s Cube. It''s designed to introduce newcomers to the process step by step.


    To
    begin, you solve the cross on one face by aligning edge pieces with the center
    color. Then, you proceed to complete the first layer by matching corner pieces
    to the adjacent edges.


    Moving on, you tackle the First Two Layers (F2L)
    step. This involves pairing up corner and edge pieces and inserting them into
    the second layer. The focus is on building blocks rather than using complex maneuvers.


    Once
    the first two layers are assembled, attention shifts to Orienting the Last Layer
    (OLL). This entails ensuring that all pieces on the last layer face the correct
    direction, sometimes requiring specific moves to achieve.


    Finally, you
    address the Permutation of the Last Layer (PLL). This stage involves rearranging
    the last layer pieces to their correct positions while maintaining their orientation.
    Algorithms are employed to achieve this without disrupting the rest of the cube.


    In
    essence, the Beginners Method serves as a foundational approach for understanding
    how to solve the Rubik''s Cube. Its simplicity provides beginners with a grasp
    of the fundamentals before delving into more advanced solving techniques.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 5302535af1044152a457ed104f1f4b91, type: 2}
